7418       data expert(type=cov);
7419       length _name_ $32 _type_ $8;
7420       infile datalines truncover;
7421       
7422       input _type_ $ _name_ $ high medium low;
7423       datalines;

NOTE: The data set WORK.EXPERT has 3 observations and 5 variables.

7427       ;
7428       data novice(type=cov);
7429       input _type_ $ _name_ $ high medium low;
7430       datalines;

NOTE: The data set WORK.NOVICE has 3 observations and 5 variables.

7434       ;
7435       proc calis;
7436       group 1 / data=expert nobs=20 label="Expert";
7437       group 2 / data=novice nobs=18 label="Novice";
7438       model 1 / groups=1,2;
7439       mstruct
7440       var=high medium low;
7441       fitindex NoIndexType On(only)=[chisq df probchi]
7442       chicorrect=eqcovmat;
7443       ods select ModelingInfo MSTRUCTVariables MSTRUCTCovInit Fit;
7444       run;

NOTE: Model 1. All lower triangular elements in the _COV_ matrix are parameters.
NOTE: The means of one or more variables in the input data set WORK.EXPERT are missing and are assumed to be 0.
NOTE: The means of one or more variables in the input data set WORK.NOVICE are missing and are assumed to be 0.
NOTE: Convergence criterion (ABSGCONV=0.00001) satisfied.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE CALIS printed pages 498-499.

7445       proc calis covpattern=eqcovmat;
7446       var high medium low;
7447       group 1 / data=expert nobs=20 label="Expert";
7448       group 2 / data=novice nobs=18 label="Novice";
7449       fitindex NoIndexType On(only)=[chisq df probchi];
7450       run;

NOTE: Group 1 is fitted by Model 1, which is defined with the COVPATTERN= or MEANPATTERN= option.
NOTE: Group 2 is fitted by Model 2, which is defined with the COVPATTERN= or MEANPATTERN= option.
NOTE: The means of one or more variables in the input data set WORK.EXPERT are missing and are assumed to be 0.
NOTE: The means of one or more variables in the input data set WORK.NOVICE are missing and are assumed to be 0.
NOTE: Convergence criterion (ABSGCONV=0.00001) satisfied.
NOTE: The chi-square correction due to Box for testing equality of covariance matrices was applied. Use the CHICORRECT=0 option if this correction is not 
      desirable.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE CALIS printed pages 500-507.

